WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:07.540
On October 5, 2017, in downtown Hereford,
England, 27-year-old Harry Godsall was going

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.280
about his day as usual.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.790
He had taken a day off from his office job
to catch up on some errands, and it was all

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.540
going swimmingly so far.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.939
He had woken up early to make a lovely cup
of tea and take his dog for a walk and had

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:26.880
noticed how nice the weather was for the time
of year, with hardly any of the usual rain.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.819
After a rich, fulfilling morning of finishing
up the dishes and laundry at his flat, he

00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:35.600
was taking a walk to the corner grocery store
to pick up some milk, potatoes, and ground

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.940
beef for the shepherd’s pie he planned to
make for dinner.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.289
All in all, it was a good day to be Harry
Godsall.

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:47.260
Surely nothing strange or unusual would come
along to derail this perfectly pleasant and

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.690
ordinary day.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.399
Out of nowhere and into what was meant to
be Harry Godsall’s day to himself suddenly

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:58.629
strolled a truly odd sight: walking down the
sidewalk toward him was a person in a full

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:03.489
spacesuit, like those worn by NASA and International
Space Station crew members.

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:08.110
In the middle of Hereford, casual as you please,
was an honest to god Spaceman.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.940
Harry attempted to walk around this bizarre
figure and carry on with his day, but it deliberately

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.750
blocked his path and spoke with a booming
voice, asking if he would be willing to join

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.520
in the fight against “the Moon Monsters.”

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.120
Well, at this point Harry had just about enough
of this nonsense and his natural penchant

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.030
for sarcasm came out.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.560
“Oh absolutely, you nutter,” he said.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.500
“I’m ready to go right now, got my toothbrush
and everything.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.500
Let’s fly, spaceman.”

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.320
He rolled his eyes, and once more attempted
to pass the astronaut.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.860
Rather than taking the hint, the figure was
overjoyed.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.020
“At last!”

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.170
It declared.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:47.030
“A brave warrior, hiding in plain sight
amidst these pastoral and bucolic humans!

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:51.350
Let us away, fair meat-fellow, and earn the
glory of heroes!

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.350
We fly!”

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:57.190
Before Harry could turn and run away from
what was certainly not an ordinary man, the

00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:02.140
spaceman grabbed him, pulling him into its
unnaturally strong arms, and activated the

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.220
jetpack strapped to its back.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:09.550
There was a massive sonic boom, shattering
every piece of glass in a 300-meter radius

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:14.470
as they took off into the sky at a speed of
25,000 kilometers per hour.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:19.480
They broke through the atmosphere and ascended
into space, so quickly that surrounding observational

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.090
satellites could not get a clear image of
the two on their journey.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:27.800
Harry Godsall had been on an ordinary quest
to have a day of chores and a hearty dinner,

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.810
and now he had vanished into outer space.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.090
His body was never found, and he could not
be positively identified on any satellite

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.090
images.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.750
The residents of Hereford had their minds
wiped with amnestics by the SCP Foundation

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.030
in order to keep the story from getting out,
and Harry Godsall was officially declared

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.030
missing.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:50.470
Three months later, when no trace of him had
surfaced, he was presumed dead.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.150
To this day, he has never been found.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.470
It is uncertain what he saw on his trip into
the stars, or what became of him.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:04.440
All that we know is, on that fateful day,
Harry encountered the entity known as SCP-1233,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.990
also known as The Lunatic or The Moon Champion.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:14.300
SCP-1233 is a humanoid entity of unknown species,
wearing a spacesuit resembling the EMU - or

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.970
Extravehicular Mobility Unit - model, complete
with an opaque visor and attached jetpack.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:24.830
The suit does not behave like an ordinary
spacesuit, capable of withstanding small-arms

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:30.520
fire, anti-tank munitions, landmine blasts,
and exposure to incredibly high temperatures

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:34.740
including complete submersion in magma without
any visible damage.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.030
No radio, microwave, or x-ray scanning has
been able to break through the material of

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.030
the suit.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:44.791
The jetpack is outfitted with a high-powered
rocket propulsion system, capable of accelerating

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:50.430
up to 40,500 kilometers per hour, at a rate
of acceleration and deceleration that should

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.040
instantly kill any human wearing it.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.090
In addition to its resilience, SCP-1233 displays
an anomalous level of physical strength, able

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:04.410
to lift and throw items up to a weight of
65,000 kilograms without exhaustion.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.980
The Moon Champion is capable of cognizant
speech and is fluent in a large number of

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:13.720
languages, able to switch its language depending
on the dominant tongue of whatever area it

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.720
is in.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.519
It communicates via a loudspeaker installed
in its suit, and speaks using flowery language

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:24.259
in a loud, authoritative voice that is usually
interpreted as male, though the gender of

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:29.389
the entity - if it even has a concept of gender
at all - is unknown.

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:34.580
It has a strong grasp of language, but, like
its behavior, its speech patterns are odd,

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.699
erratic, and sometimes completely impossible
to understand.

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:43.520
SCP-1233 appears every 4-5 years, each time
following a similar pattern.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.220
First, the entity will fall from an unknown
height above the surface of the earth, falling

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.809
at a terminal velocity similar to that of
a small meteorite or a vehicle re-entering

00:04:52.809 --> 00:04:54.860
the atmosphere.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.800
As it falls, SCP-1233 will emit red-orange
thermal radiance, causing it to be mistaken

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:03.020
for a shooting star if its descent occurs
at night.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.849
Then, it will crash-land on the ground, leaving
a large crater and causing a small earthquake

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:09.080
in the vicinity.

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:14.229
It tends to land within 7 to 30 kilometers
from a town, usually a smaller municipality

00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:16.970
with a population of 30,000 or less.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.879
Then, 1233 will climb out of its crater and
head toward the town on foot or by flight.

00:05:21.879 --> 00:05:27.270
It does not ordinarily head directly to the
town and has been observed taking its time,

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:32.340
taking the “scenic route” if you will,
and engaging in a variety of random detours.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:38.680
SCP-1233 has taken the time to inspect various
objects, including farm equipment, buildings,

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.210
and plants.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.419
Occasionally it will pick these plants, and
has been observed plucking the petals from

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:48.590
a flower in what can only be identified as
an interplanetary variation on the classic

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:51.559
“he loves me, he loves me not” game.

00:05:51.559 --> 00:05:55.749
Sometimes it will chase after insects, such
as grasshoppers and butterflies, demanding

00:05:55.749 --> 00:05:58.339
that they stop and allow the entity to observe
them.

00:05:58.339 --> 00:06:03.409
Once, it accidentally crushed a ladybug between
its hands and wept inconsolably for a duration

00:06:03.409 --> 00:06:05.559
of 25 straight minutes.

00:06:05.559 --> 00:06:10.190
In addition to interacting with insects, it
also attempts to speak to various animals.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:14.460
It has been spotted attempting to interrogate
a cow about its motives, greeting a bird as

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.939
if it were the owner of a house it was perched
on the roof of, and asking a frog where the

00:06:18.939 --> 00:06:22.039
nearest place to get “something good to
eat” was.

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:25.580
It is unknown what, or even if, the entity
eats.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.810
It has been seen pulling root vegetables from
the ground or picking fruit from bushes and

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.639
trees and shoving them directly into its closed
visor, crushing them uselessly, in what seems

00:06:34.639 --> 00:06:36.389
to be an attempt to eat them.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:38.280
Naturally, this attempt is fruitless.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.080
Do you get it?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.080
My joke?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.080
Fruitless?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.080
Cause he- Ahem.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.080
Anyway.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.640
When it is not attempting to eat, or interact
with new life forms, SCP-1233 occasionally

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.740
will march directly into large bodies of water
such as lakes or ponds, then emerge from them

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.780
and shake the water off of its suit.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:59.960
It will also stand completely still for durations
of up to several hours.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.160
The reason for any of this behavior, like
basically everything else about the entity,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.840
is unknown.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.559
Once SCP-1233 has reached the limits of the
town, it will attempt to engage with the population.

00:07:11.559 --> 00:07:16.190
Due to its curious nature, heightened strength,
and lack of any understanding of proper human

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:21.849
behavior, this often results in confusion,
disruption, and a great deal of property damage.

00:07:21.849 --> 00:07:26.930
A typical example of SCP-1233’s interaction
with the general public is found in archived

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:32.539
security camera footage from a bakery in Saratoga
Springs, New York by the name of “Sam’s

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:33.539
Sweets.”

00:07:33.539 --> 00:07:40.830
On August 9, 2009, SCP-1233 entered the café
and attempted to speak with its co-owner,

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.259
32-year-old Bob Parsons.

00:07:42.259 --> 00:07:46.800
Parsons greeted the entity with a friendly,
if perplexed, attitude, presuming it to be

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.659
a cosplayer taking a snack break from a nearby
comic book convention.

00:07:50.659 --> 00:07:56.179
The entity identified itself as “Moon Champion,
champion of the moon, defender of space justice

00:07:56.179 --> 00:07:57.809
and destroyer of evil.”

00:07:57.809 --> 00:08:02.919
After introducing itself, SCP-1233 asked Bob
if he was the President of Earth.

00:08:02.919 --> 00:08:07.309
He was understandably amused by the question,
laughing hard enough to bring tears to his

00:08:07.309 --> 00:08:11.349
eyes, and offered the entity a free cookie
in exchange for cheering him up.

00:08:11.349 --> 00:08:16.589
SCP-1233 identified the cookie - incorrectly,
obviously - as a parakeet, and smashed the

00:08:16.589 --> 00:08:21.629
confection uselessly into its unopened visor,
scattering crumbs all over the counter and

00:08:21.629 --> 00:08:22.629
floor.

00:08:22.629 --> 00:08:26.599
It then attempted to engage Bob in conversation
about the “moon monsters” that it was

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:31.270
dedicated to fighting in its homeland: “the
majestic and magnificent Moon Kingdom.”

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:37.349
SCP-1233 then asked if it could perhaps befriend
a dog and take it back to the moon, and attempted

00:08:37.349 --> 00:08:41.130
to recruit Bob to fight alongside it against
the Moon Monsters.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:45.410
Bob, with a great deal of polite confusion,
insisted that he had to stay on earth and

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.810
continue to run the bakery in order to keep
the citizens fed.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:53.209
1233 thanked him for his time, bid him farewell,
and crashed through a concrete wall leaving

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:55.779
a distinct astronaut-shaped hole.

00:08:55.779 --> 00:09:00.980
SCP-1233 spent the rest of the day wandering
into traffic and causing several accidents,

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:05.600
breaking through glass storefronts, challenging
a fire hydrant to hand-to-hand combat, making

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.000
a pile of stolen bicycles in the middle of
a public park, and collecting as many dogs

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.339
as it could hold, then attempting to use said
dogs as a type of currency to purchase even

00:09:14.339 --> 00:09:16.370
more dogs.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:23.019
Finally, after leaving all of this head scratch-inducing
destruction in its wake, SCP-1233 activated

00:09:23.019 --> 00:09:28.060
its jetpack and took off out of the Earth’s
atmosphere, apparently returning to the Moon.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:32.880
None of SCP-1233’s claims about the moon
have been verified, though the Foundation

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.470
maintains contact with Lunar Area-32 to keep
an eye out for Moon People, a Moon Kingdom,

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.079
and the Moon Monsters 1233 spoke of.

00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:46.510
In the meantime, the Foundation is simply
doing its best to contain SCP-1233 and minimize

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.810
its damage as much as possible.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:53.820
Because of the anomalous physical properties
of SCP-1233, there is no way to physically

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:56.420
contain it at this point in time.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.829
Until a method of physical containment can
be found, secondary measures will be taken

00:10:00.829 --> 00:10:04.120
to keep this lunar lunatic from causing any
more havoc.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.199
Or, at the very least, reduce its levels of
havoc as much as possible.

00:10:08.199 --> 00:10:11.850
There’s only so much havoc we can prevent
in this world, especially when you have an

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:15.740
astronaut plummeting from the sky on a semi-regular
basis.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:20.569
The Foundation satellite observation network
ARGOS, or Atmospheric Reconnaissance Global

00:10:20.569 --> 00:10:26.339
Observation System, enters priority 2 high
alert status once 3 years and 6 months have

00:10:26.339 --> 00:10:28.899
passed since SCP-1233’s last appearance.

00:10:28.899 --> 00:10:34.269
When 1233 is spotted in the upper thermosphere,
a Foundation Mobile Task Force will be deployed

00:10:34.269 --> 00:10:38.459
in whatever populated area is closest to the
entity’s estimated landing point.

00:10:38.459 --> 00:10:43.410
There, they will prepare to administer amnestics
and provide a cover story - such as: immersive

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:49.750
theatre piece, prank show, 2001: A Space Odyssey
remake - to any civilians who witness SCP-1233’s

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.850
arrival.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:54.910
In addition to these measures, there is to
be a media blackout in place in order to prevent

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.690
knowledge of 1233 from spreading.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:11:01.519
Task Force operatives are authorized to grab
the smartphones of any bystanders attempting

00:11:01.519 --> 00:11:06.450
to take photos, videos, tiktoks, or any other
documentation of the entity, and promptly

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.910
smash them on the ground in front of them.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.089
It’s not like they’re going to stay mad,
they’re all getting their memories wiped

00:11:12.089 --> 00:11:13.089
anyway.

00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:18.830
If SCP-1233 stays in the area for an unusually
long amount of time, a mass amnesticization

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:22.040
of the town or city where it landed may be
authorized.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:25.930
Though the task force is permitted to interact
with civilians in order to slow the spread

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:30.720
of information and provide cover stories,
no interaction between Foundation personnel

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.320
and SCP-1233 is permitted under any circumstances.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.470
Even if they think it would be really funny.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:42.709
No matter how epic your moon man prank might
be, it is never worth your life.

00:11:42.709 --> 00:11:45.160
Now go check out “NASA Lies?

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:51.160
SCP-2001 - Space Oddity” and “How To Actually
Beat SCP-3008 The Infinite Ikea” for more

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.750
SCP videos that’ll make you laugh rather
than scream!

